--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Saturday, the 3rd of January, 1931 (3/3 key facts kept) ---
I redeemed Fred's watch from the pawnbroker for eleven shillings.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Saturday, the 3rd of January, 1931 (0/2 key facts kept) ---
I read in the Daily Herald that 150,000 miners in South Wales are idle, and little activity is reported in the great collieries.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Saturday, the 3rd of January, 1931 (2/2 key facts kept) ---
To-day I received three letters from Mr. Arthur Hale, and found the quarterly ledger not finished. I resolved that in future the ledger must be completed before the close of business on Friday evenings, and wrote to Mr. Hale accordingly.
   ☾ Ada: She dreamt that her husband, who had been dead nine years, came to her, and kissed her.
   ☾ Arthur: He dreamt that he was walking with Mr. Thomas in a public place, and Mr. Thomas suddenly turned upon him and rated him soundly for being behindhand with his work.
   ☾ Mr. Thomas: He dreamt that Hale was promoted to be chief clerk.

