--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (4/6 key facts kept) ---
To-day I pawned my wedding ring for 5s. Od., to redeem my husband's watch from pawn.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (4/4 key facts kept) ---
To-day I balanced the quarterly ledger, and made an error in one of the totals. I resolved never to make an entry in the books of the company, except under my personal supervision; and Mr. Thomas examined the ledger and found the three totals not quite finished.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (2/2 key facts kept) ---
To-day I received three letters from Mr. Arthur Hale, of which the first two were short, and the last a little longer. I examined the quarterly ledger kept by him, and found them not finished; so I resolved that in future they must be concluded before the business of the day concludes.
   ☾ Ada (forgotten by morning): She dreamt that she saw her sister Lizzie walking in a field at Paddock Wood, with a baby in her arms.
   ☾ Arthur (forgotten by morning): He dreamt that he was in a great city, and walked along a street, thronged with people, all running one way.
   ☾ Mr. Thomas (forgotten by morning): He dreamt that he was walking down Oxford Street, and saw a member of Parliament, whom he knew, going into a public-house.

